		<title type="html"><![CDATA[Réponse à&#160;:  Problème pour créer collation]]></title>
		<link rel="alternate" href="http://forums.postgresql.fr/viewtopic.php?pid=27368#p27368"/>
		<content type="html"><![CDATA[<p>Je viens de tester à la main, j’ai ce retour erreur :</p><p>New collation French_France.1252 is incompatible with the collation of the template database &lt;C&gt;.<br />Use the same collation as in the template database&#160; or use template 0 as template.</p><p>Ma commande sql était : <br />Create database Jeremy <br />With owner jeremy <br />Encoding =‘UTF8’<br />Tablespace =pg_default <br />LC_COLLATE= ´French_France.1252’<br />LC_CTYPE = ´French_France.1252’<br />Connection limit = -1;</p>]]></content>
		<author>
			<name><![CDATA[GDS_Strou]]></name>
			<uri>http://forums.postgresql.fr/profile.php?id=8057</uri>
		</author>
		<updated>2018-04-23T14:42:27Z</updated>
		<id>http://forums.postgresql.fr/viewtopic.php?pid=27368#p27368</id>
	</entry>
	<entry>
		<title type="html"><![CDATA[Réponse à&#160;:  Problème pour créer collation]]></title>
		<link rel="alternate" href="http://forums.postgresql.fr/viewtopic.php?pid=27366#p27366"/>
		<content type="html"><![CDATA[<p>Il se trouve que la locale French_France.1252 n&#039;est pas limitée à un encodage spécifique. Comme dit dans la doc ici:</p><p><a href="https://www.postgresql.org/docs/current/static/multibyte.html" rel="nofollow">https://www.postgresql.org/docs/current … ibyte.html</a></p><div class="quotebox"><blockquote><div><p>For C or POSIX locale, any character set is allowed, but for other libc-provided locales there is only one character set that will work correctly. <br />(<strong>On Windows, however, UTF-8 encoding can be used with any locale.</strong>) If you have ICU support configured, ICU-provided locales can be used with most but not all server-side encodings.</p></div></blockquote></div><p>Si pgAdmin ne propose pas la collation nouvellement créee, le problème est à son niveau.</p><p>Un CREATE DATABASE à la main devrait passer.</p>]]></content>
